# The verification samples are hashed, so their bytes must survive a clone unchanged.
#
# Git's default on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For an ordinary source file
# that is harmless; for these it is fatal. Every one of them is committed to by a SHA-256
# in an on-chain receipt, so a single rewritten line ending changes the hash and the
# verifier correctly reports that the result does not match — on a repository whose whole
# claim is that it does. Someone cloning on Windows would see VOID on an honest receipt
# and have no way to tell why.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions and leaves the bytes alone.
samples/** -text

# Fonts, artwork and screenshots are binary and must never be touched either.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
